{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015XWhFzMye9mdCnU2EUBVzN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-vna — Requirements: M1 Strategy 1 — Triple Screen Strategy (Alexander Elder)\n2\t\n3\t**Issue:** QuantAgent-vna  \n4\t**Parent:** QuantAgent-l0h (AC3)  \n5\t**Type:** Requirements  \n6\t**Created:** 2026-05-05  \n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## Objective\n11\t\n12\tImplement the Triple Screen trading system by Alexander Elder as M1 Strategy 1. The strategy must integrate cleanly with the existing `TradingStrategy` abstraction and be exercisable by the current `Backtest` engine with no changes to shared infrastructure.\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## Scope In\n17\t\n18\t- New file `quantagent/strategy/triple_screen_strategy.py` implementing `TripleScreenStrategy(TradingStrategy)`\n19\t- Unit tests covering all three screens independently and their combined signal logic\n20\t- Reference backtest profile in the implementation doc (IM)\n21\t- Entry in `quantagent/strategy/__init__.py` (or equivalent export)\n22\t\n23\t## Scope Out\n24\t\n25\t- Changes to `backtest.py`, `assembler.py`, `base.py`, or any other shared module\n26\t- Multi-timeframe live data fetching (the strategy simulates multi-TF via bar aggregation)\n27\t- Parameter optimization per asset\n28\t- Comparison against other strategies\n29\t\n30\t---\n31\t\n32\t## Background — Triple Screen System\n33\t\n34\tTriple Screen (Elder, 1986) filters entries through three sequential screens to reduce false signals:\n35\t\n36\t| Screen | Purpose | Classic indicators |\n37\t|--------|---------|-------------------|\n38\t| 1 | Dominant trend on a higher timeframe | MACD histogram slope, EMA slope |\n39\t| 2 | Pullback/rally oscillator on intermediate TF | Stochastic, Force Index |\n40\t| 3 | Entry trigger on lowest TF | Breakout above/below prior bar high/low |\n41\t\n42\tOnly trades aligned with Screen 1's trend direction that also pass Screen 2's oscillator filter and Screen 3's trigger are executed.\n43\t\n44\t---\n45\t\n46\t## Functional Requirements\n47\t\n48\t### FR1 — Strategy class\n49\tA `TripleScreenStrategy` class must exist in `quantagent/strategy/triple_screen_strategy.py` and implement the full `TradingStrategy` ABC (`generate_signal`, `should_reevaluate`).\n50\t\n51\t### FR2 — Configurable parameters\n52\tThe constructor must accept at minimum:\n53\t\n54\t| Parameter | Default | Description |\n55\t|-----------|---------|-------------|\n56\t| `weekly_bars` | 5 | Number of input candles to aggregate into one \"higher-TF bar\" for Screen 1 |\n57\t| `trend_ema_period` | 13 | EMA period computed on the aggregated (weekly) bars |\n58\t| `stoch_k_period` | 5 | Stochastic %K lookback on the intermediate-TF candles |\n59\t| `stoch_d_period` | 3 | Signal line smoothing for %D |\n60\t| `stoch_oversold` | 20.0 | %K threshold below which a pullback is confirmed (uptrend entries) |\n61\t| `stoch_overbought` | 80.0 | %K threshold above which a rally is confirmed (downtrend entries) |\n62\t| `stop_loss_pct` | 0.02 | Fixed stop loss as a fraction of entry price |\n63\t| `take_profit_pct` | 0.04 | Fixed take profit as a fraction of entry price |\n64\t| `trailing_stop_pct` | 0.05 | Trailing stop fraction passed through to `TradingSignal` |\n65\t\n66\t### FR3 — Screen 1: weekly trend filter\n67\t`generate_signal()` must aggregate the input `kline_data` into blocks of `weekly_bars` candles to form synthetic higher-TF bars (OHLCV aggregation: open=first, high=max, low=min, close=last, volume=sum). It then computes an EMA of `trend_ema_period` on the synthetic bars' close prices and determines trend direction from the slope of the last two EMA values:\n68\t\n69\t- Slope > 0 → uptrend\n70\t- Slope < 0 → downtrend\n71\t- Insufficient data → return `None` (no signal)\n72\t\n73\t### FR4 — Screen 2: stochastic pullback/rally filter\n74\tOn the original input candles (not aggregated), compute Stochastic %K and %D over `stoch_k_period` / `stoch_d_period`:\n75\t\n76\t- In uptrend: the screen is \"activated\" when the most recent %K is below `stoch_oversold`\n77\t- In downtrend: the screen is \"activated\" when the most recent %K is above `stoch_overbought`\n78\t- If the screen is not activated, return `None`\n79\t\n80\t### FR5 — Screen 3: breakout entry trigger\n81\tIf Screens 1 and 2 both pass, use the most recent completed candle as the trigger:\n82\t\n83\t- Uptrend + oversold %K: signal `LONG` when `current_price > kline_data[-2][\"high\"]` (breakout above prior bar high)\n84\t- Downtrend + overbought %K: signal `SHORT` when `current_price < kline_data[-2][\"low\"]` (breakout below prior bar low)\n85\t- If the price has not broken out, return `None` (wait for trigger)\n86\t\n87\t### FR6 — Minimum data guard\n88\t`generate_signal()` must return `None` without raising when `len(kline_data)` is less than the minimum required:\n89\t\n90\t```\n91\tmin_candles = weekly_bars * trend_ema_period + stoch_k_period + stoch_d_period\n92\t```\n93\t\n94\tWith defaults that is `5 × 13 + 5 + 3 = 73` candles.\n95\t\n96\t### FR7 — Signal construction\n97\tWhen all three screens pass, produce a `TradingSignal` with:\n98\t\n99\t- `decision`: \"LONG\" or \"SHORT\"\n100\t- `confidence`: normalised value derived from how extreme %K is (deeper oversold/overbought → higher confidence), clamped to [0.1, 1.0]\n101\t- `entry_price`: `current_price`\n102\t- `stop_loss`: entry ± `stop_loss_pct` (long: below, short: above)\n103\t- `take_profit`: entry ± `take_profit_pct` (long: above, short: below)\n104\t- `reasoning`: human-readable string naming active screens and indicator values\n105\t- `exit_policy`: `ExitPolicy.TRAILING_STOP`\n106\t- `trailing_stop_pct`: `trailing_stop_pct`\n107\t\n108\t### FR8 — `should_reevaluate` behaviour\n109\tReturn `False`; the strategy does not re-evaluate once a position is open (same contract as `RSIMeanReversionStrategy`).\n110\t\n111\t---\n112\t\n113\t## Edge Cases\n114\t\n115\t- Fewer candles than `min_candles` → return `None`, no exception\n116\t- EMA slope exactly 0 → treat as downtrend (neutral → skip to avoid whipsaws)\n117\t- %K equal to threshold boundary → inclusive comparison (`<=` for oversold, `>=` for overbought)\n118\t- Aggregation remainder (candles not divisible by `weekly_bars`) → ignore the tail, use only complete blocks\n119\t- `kline_data[-2]` access: validated via the minimum candle guard (always safe when guard passes)\n120\t\n121\t---\n122\t\n123\t## Definition of Done\n124\t\n125\t- `TripleScreenStrategy` class exists and all three screen methods are independently testable\n126\t- Default parameters chosen are documented here (above)\n127\t- Unit tests in `tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py` exercise each screen's pass/fail independently and the combined logic\n128\t- A reference backtest profile is documented in the IM doc and a run confirms PnL is calculated and no crashes occur\n129\t- `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-vna-AC-triple-screen-strategy.md` is complete and aligned\n130\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e29365a-7925-40eb-8646-1f5eb6603bf2","uuid":"7312e615-cabc-4970-97af-91575903ec36","timestamp":"2026-05-05T12:45:03.264Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/01_requirements/QuantAgent-vna-RQ-triple-screen-strategy.md","content":"# QuantAgent-vna — Requirements: M1 Strategy 1 — Triple Screen Strategy (Alexander Elder)\n\n**Issue:** QuantAgent-vna  \n**Parent:** QuantAgent-l0h (AC3)  \n**Type:** Requirements  \n**Created:** 2026-05-05  \n\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nImplement the Triple Screen trading system by Alexander Elder as M1 Strategy 1. The strategy must integrate cleanly with the existing `TradingStrategy` abstraction and be exercisable by the current `Backtest` engine with no changes to shared infrastructure.\n\n---\n\n## Scope In\n\n- New file `quantagent/strategy/triple_screen_strategy.py` implementing `TripleScreenStrategy(TradingStrategy)`\n- Unit tests covering all three screens independently and their combined signal logic\n- Reference backtest profile in the implementation doc (IM)\n- Entry in `quantagent/strategy/__init__.py` (or equivalent export)\n\n## Scope Out\n\n- Changes to `backtest.py`, `assembler.py`, `base.py`, or any other shared module\n- Multi-timeframe live data fetching (the strategy simulates multi-TF via bar aggregation)\n- Parameter optimization per asset\n- Comparison against other strategies\n\n---\n\n## Background — Triple Screen System\n\nTriple Screen (Elder, 1986) filters entries through three sequential screens to reduce false signals:\n\n| Screen | Purpose | Classic indicators |\n|--------|---------|-------------------|\n| 1 | Dominant trend on a higher timeframe | MACD histogram slope, EMA slope |\n| 2 | Pullback/rally oscillator on intermediate TF | Stochastic, Force Index |\n| 3 | Entry trigger on lowest TF | Breakout above/below prior bar high/low |\n\nOnly trades aligned with Screen 1's trend direction that also pass Screen 2's oscillator filter and Screen 3's trigger are executed.\n\n---\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR1 — Strategy class\nA `TripleScreenStrategy` class must exist in `quantagent/strategy/triple_screen_strategy.py` and implement the full `TradingStrategy` ABC (`generate_signal`, `should_reevaluate`).\n\n### FR2 — Configurable parameters\nThe constructor must accept at minimum:\n\n| Parameter | Default | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-------------|\n| `weekly_bars` | 5 | Number of input candles to aggregate into one \"higher-TF bar\" for Screen 1 |\n| `trend_ema_period` | 13 | EMA period computed on the aggregated (weekly) bars |\n| `stoch_k_period` | 5 | Stochastic %K lookback on the intermediate-TF candles |\n| `stoch_d_period` | 3 | Signal line smoothing for %D |\n| `stoch_oversold` | 20.0 | %K threshold below which a pullback is confirmed (uptrend entries) |\n| `stoch_overbought` | 80.0 | %K threshold above which a rally is confirmed (downtrend entries) |\n| `stop_loss_pct` | 0.02 | Fixed stop loss as a fraction of entry price |\n| `take_profit_pct` | 0.04 | Fixed take profit as a fraction of entry price |\n| `trailing_stop_pct` | 0.05 | Trailing stop fraction passed through to `TradingSignal` |\n\n### FR3 — Screen 1: weekly trend filter\n`generate_signal()` must aggregate the input `kline_data` into blocks of `weekly_bars` candles to form synthetic higher-TF bars (OHLCV aggregation: open=first, high=max, low=min, close=last, volume=sum). It then computes an EMA of `trend_ema_period` on the synthetic bars' close prices and determines trend direction from the slope of the last two EMA values:\n\n- Slope > 0 → uptrend\n- Slope < 0 → downtrend\n- Insufficient data → return `None` (no signal)\n\n### FR4 — Screen 2: stochastic pullback/rally filter\nOn the original input candles (not aggregated), compute Stochastic %K and %D over `stoch_k_period` / `stoch_d_period`:\n\n- In uptrend: the screen is \"activated\" when the most recent %K is below `stoch_oversold`\n- In downtrend: the screen is \"activated\" when the most recent %K is above `stoch_overbought`\n- If the screen is not activated, return `None`\n\n### FR5 — Screen 3: breakout entry trigger\nIf Screens 1 and 2 both pass, use the most recent completed candle as the trigger:\n\n- Uptrend + oversold %K: signal `LONG` when `current_price > kline_data[-2][\"high\"]` (breakout above prior bar high)\n- Downtrend + overbought %K: signal `SHORT` when `current_price < kline_data[-2][\"low\"]` (breakout below prior bar low)\n- If the price has not broken out, return `None` (wait for trigger)\n\n### FR6 — Minimum data guard\n`generate_signal()` must return `None` without raising when `len(kline_data)` is less than the minimum required:\n\n```\nmin_candles = weekly_bars * trend_ema_period + stoch_k_period + stoch_d_period\n```\n\nWith defaults that is `5 × 13 + 5 + 3 = 73` candles.\n\n### FR7 — Signal construction\nWhen all three screens pass, produce a `TradingSignal` with:\n\n- `decision`: \"LONG\" or \"SHORT\"\n- `confidence`: normalised value derived from how extreme %K is (deeper oversold/overbought → higher confidence), clamped to [0.1, 1.0]\n- `entry_price`: `current_price`\n- `stop_loss`: entry ± `stop_loss_pct` (long: below, short: above)\n- `take_profit`: entry ± `take_profit_pct` (long: above, short: below)\n- `reasoning`: human-readable string naming active screens and indicator values\n- `exit_policy`: `ExitPolicy.TRAILING_STOP`\n- `trailing_stop_pct`: `trailing_stop_pct`\n\n### FR8 — `should_reevaluate` behaviour\nReturn `False`; the strategy does not re-evaluate once a position is open (same contract as `RSIMeanReversionStrategy`).\n\n---\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Fewer candles than `min_candles` → return `None`, no exception\n- EMA slope exactly 0 → treat as downtrend (neutral → skip to avoid whipsaws)\n- %K equal to threshold boundary → inclusive comparison (`<=` for oversold, `>=` for overbought)\n- Aggregation remainder (candles not divisible by `weekly_bars`) → ignore the tail, use only complete blocks\n- `kline_data[-2]` access: validated via the minimum candle guard (always safe when guard passes)\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- `TripleScreenStrategy` class exists and all three screen methods are independently testable\n- Default parameters chosen are documented here (above)\n- Unit tests in `tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py` exercise each screen's pass/fail independently and the combined logic\n- A reference backtest profile is documented in the IM doc and a run confirms PnL is calculated and no crashes occur\n- `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-vna-AC-triple-screen-strategy.md` is complete and aligned\n","numLines":130,"startLine":1,"totalLines":130}}}
