{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QGv8Vhka41wn33RKBZykyx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-vna — Acceptance Criteria: M1 Strategy 1 — Triple Screen Strategy\n2\t\n3\t**Issue:** QuantAgent-vna  \n4\t**Parent:** QuantAgent-l0h (AC3)  \n5\t**Type:** Acceptance Tests  \n6\t**Created:** 2026-05-05  \n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## AC1 — Strategy class exists and satisfies the `TradingStrategy` ABC\n11\t\n12\t**Given** `quantagent/strategy/triple_screen_strategy.py` is present in the repo  \n13\t**When** `from quantagent.strategy.triple_screen_strategy import TripleScreenStrategy` is executed  \n14\t**Then**:\n15\t- No import errors\n16\t- `issubclass(TripleScreenStrategy, TradingStrategy)` is `True`\n17\t- Instantiation with default parameters succeeds: `TripleScreenStrategy()`\n18\t\n19\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py::test_class_is_valid_strategy`\n20\t\n21\t---\n22\t\n23\t## AC2 — Screen 1: EMA slope correctly identifies trend direction\n24\t\n25\t### AC2.1 — Rising EMA slope → uptrend\n26\t\n27\t**Given** synthetic weekly bars whose close prices strictly increase over the last `trend_ema_period + 1` bars  \n28\t**When** `_screen1_trend()` is called with those bars  \n29\t**Then** the return value is `\"UP\"`\n30\t\n31\t### AC2.2 — Falling EMA slope → downtrend\n32\t\n33\t**Given** synthetic weekly bars whose close prices strictly decrease  \n34\t**When** `_screen1_trend()` is called  \n35\t**Then** the return value is `\"DOWN\"`\n36\t\n37\t### AC2.3 — Insufficient weekly bars → None\n38\t\n39\t**Given** fewer than `trend_ema_period + 1` synthetic weekly bars  \n40\t**When** `_screen1_trend()` is called  \n41\t**Then** the return value is `None`\n42\t\n43\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py -k \"screen1\"`\n44\t\n45\t---\n46\t\n47\t## AC3 — Screen 2: Stochastic oscillator activates correctly\n48\t\n49\t### AC3.1 — Uptrend + oversold %K → screen activated\n50\t\n51\t**Given** a candle series where the last few closes are near the period low (deep pullback)  \n52\t  and trend is `\"UP\"`  \n53\t**When** `_screen2_oscillator()` is called  \n54\t**Then** the screen returns `True` (buy setup confirmed)\n55\t\n56\t### AC3.2 — Uptrend + %K above oversold threshold → screen not activated\n57\t\n58\t**Given** a candle series where %K is above `stoch_oversold`  \n59\t  and trend is `\"UP\"`  \n60\t**When** `_screen2_oscillator()` is called  \n61\t**Then** the screen returns `False`\n62\t\n63\t### AC3.3 — Downtrend + overbought %K → screen activated\n64\t\n65\t**Given** a candle series where the last few closes are near the period high (rally in downtrend)  \n66\t  and trend is `\"DOWN\"`  \n67\t**When** `_screen2_oscillator()` is called  \n68\t**Then** the screen returns `True` (short setup confirmed)\n69\t\n70\t### AC3.4 — Downtrend + %K below overbought threshold → screen not activated\n71\t\n72\t**Given** a candle series where %K is below `stoch_overbought`  \n73\t  and trend is `\"DOWN\"`  \n74\t**When** `_screen2_oscillator()` is called  \n75\t**Then** the screen returns `False`\n76\t\n77\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py -k \"screen2\"`\n78\t\n79\t---\n80\t\n81\t## AC4 — Screen 3: Breakout trigger fires correctly\n82\t\n83\t### AC4.1 — Uptrend + breakout above prior high → LONG trigger\n84\t\n85\t**Given** trend is `\"UP\"`, Screen 2 activated, and `current_price > kline_data[-2][\"high\"]`  \n86\t**When** `_screen3_trigger()` is called  \n87\t**Then** the return value is `True`\n88\t\n89\t### AC4.2 — Uptrend + no breakout → no trigger\n90\t\n91\t**Given** trend is `\"UP\"`, Screen 2 activated, but `current_price <= kline_data[-2][\"high\"]`  \n92\t**When** `_screen3_trigger()` is called  \n93\t**Then** the return value is `False`\n94\t\n95\t### AC4.3 — Downtrend + breakout below prior low → SHORT trigger\n96\t\n97\t**Given** trend is `\"DOWN\"`, Screen 2 activated, and `current_price < kline_data[-2][\"low\"]`  \n98\t**When** `_screen3_trigger()` is called  \n99\t**Then** the return value is `True`\n100\t\n101\t### AC4.4 — Downtrend + no breakout → no trigger\n102\t\n103\t**Given** trend is `\"DOWN\"`, Screen 2 activated, but `current_price >= kline_data[-2][\"low\"]`  \n104\t**When** `_screen3_trigger()` is called  \n105\t**Then** the return value is `False`\n106\t\n107\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py -k \"screen3\"`\n108\t\n109\t---\n110\t\n111\t## AC5 — Combined: `generate_signal` produces correct decisions\n112\t\n113\t### AC5.1 — All three screens pass (uptrend) → LONG signal\n114\t\n115\t**Given** deterministic kline_data where:\n116\t- EMA slope is rising (Screen 1 = UP)\n117\t- Stochastic %K < `stoch_oversold` (Screen 2 activated)\n118\t- `current_price > kline_data[-2][\"high\"]` (Screen 3 triggered)\n119\t\n120\t**When** `strategy.generate_signal(kline_data, \"BTC-USD\", \"4h\", current_price)` is called  \n121\t**Then**:\n122\t- Return value is a `TradingSignal` (not None)\n123\t- `signal.decision == \"LONG\"`\n124\t- `signal.confidence` is in `[0.1, 1.0]`\n125\t- `signal.entry_price == current_price`\n126\t- `signal.stop_loss == current_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct)` (within float tolerance)\n127\t- `signal.take_profit == current_price * (1 + take_profit_pct)` (within float tolerance)\n128\t- `signal.reasoning` contains \"Screen\" (screens are named in the reasoning string)\n129\t\n130\t### AC5.2 — All three screens pass (downtrend) → SHORT signal\n131\t\n132\t**Given** deterministic kline_data where:\n133\t- EMA slope is falling (Screen 1 = DOWN)\n134\t- Stochastic %K > `stoch_overbought` (Screen 2 activated)\n135\t- `current_price < kline_data[-2][\"low\"]` (Screen 3 triggered)\n136\t\n137\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n138\t**Then**:\n139\t- `signal.decision == \"SHORT\"`\n140\t- `signal.stop_loss == current_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct)`\n141\t- `signal.take_profit == current_price * (1 - take_profit_pct)`\n142\t\n143\t### AC5.3 — Screen 1 passes but Screen 2 does not activate → `None`\n144\t\n145\t**Given** EMA slope rising (UP) but stochastic %K is well above `stoch_oversold`  \n146\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n147\t**Then** return value is `None`\n148\t\n149\t### AC5.4 — Screens 1 and 2 pass but Screen 3 does not fire → `None`\n150\t\n151\t**Given** EMA slope rising (UP), %K below `stoch_oversold`, but `current_price <= kline_data[-2][\"high\"]`  \n152\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n153\t**Then** return value is `None`\n154\t\n155\t### AC5.5 — Fewer than min candles → `None` without exception\n156\t\n157\t**Given** `len(kline_data) < weekly_bars * (trend_ema_period + 1) + stoch_k_period + stoch_d_period`  \n158\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n159\t**Then** return value is `None` and no exception is raised\n160\t\n161\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py -k \"generate_signal\"`\n162\t\n163\t---\n164\t\n165\t## AC6 — Non-HOLD signals are generated in a realistic market scenario\n166\t\n167\t**Given** a synthetic 200-candle 4h dataset designed with a clear trend + pullback + breakout pattern  \n168\t**When** `generate_signal()` is called on the last candle  \n169\t**Then** the return value is a `TradingSignal` (not `None`), proving the strategy is not permanently stuck in HOLD\n170\t\n171\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py::test_generates_signal_in_realistic_scenario`\n172\t\n173\t---\n174\t\n175\t## AC7 — Reference backtest completes without crash and PnL is calculated\n176\t\n177\t**Given** a test environment with:\n178\t- PostgreSQL or SQLite database configured\n179\t- Market data available for BTCUSD, timeframe 4h, 2024-01-01 to 2024-03-31\n180\t\n181\t**When** the reference backtest from `QuantAgent-vna-IM` is run:\n182\t```python\n183\tstrategy = TripleScreenStrategy()\n184\tbacktest = Backtest(\n185\t    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n186\t    end_date=datetime(2024, 3, 31),\n187\t    assets=[\"BTC-USD\"],\n188\t    timeframe=\"4h\",\n189\t    initial_capital=100_000.0,\n190\t    strategy=strategy,\n191\t)\n192\tmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"QuantAgent-vna-reference\")\n193\t```\n194\t\n195\t**Then**:\n196\t- `backtest.run()` completes without raising any exception\n197\t- `metrics.total_pnl` is a finite float (positive, negative, or zero)\n198\t- `metrics.total_trades >= 0`\n199\t- The run is logged with a name containing \"QuantAgent-vna\"\n200\t\n201\t**Testable:** Manual integration test or `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py::test_backtest_integration -m integration`\n202\t\n203\t---\n204\t\n205\t## AC8 — `should_reevaluate` always returns False\n206\t\n207\t**Given** any `ActivePosition` and `current_price`  \n208\t**When** `strategy.should_reevaluate(position, current_price)` is called  \n209\t**Then** the return value is `False`\n210\t\n211\t**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py::test_should_reevaluate_false`\n212\t\n213\t---\n214\t\n215\t## Non-goals (explicitly excluded)\n216\t\n217\t- Performance targets (win rate, Sharpe ratio, drawdown)\n218\t- Multi-symbol parallel backtesting validation\n219\t- Provider-specific behaviour or LLM integration\n220\t- Comparison against RSI or LLMAgentStrategy results\n221\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e29365a-7925-40eb-8646-1f5eb6603bf2","uuid":"40a857ae-4efd-49c9-a875-fa14646bb139","timestamp":"2026-05-05T12:45:14.865Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-vna-AC-triple-screen-strategy.md","content":"# QuantAgent-vna — Acceptance Criteria: M1 Strategy 1 — Triple Screen Strategy\n\n**Issue:** QuantAgent-vna  \n**Parent:** QuantAgent-l0h (AC3)  \n**Type:** Acceptance Tests  \n**Created:** 2026-05-05  \n\n---\n\n## AC1 — Strategy class exists and satisfies the `TradingStrategy` ABC\n\n**Given** `quantagent/strategy/triple_screen_strategy.py` is present in the repo  \n**When** `from quantagent.strategy.triple_screen_strategy import TripleScreenStrategy` is executed  \n**Then**:\n- No import errors\n- `issubclass(TripleScreenStrategy, TradingStrategy)` is `True`\n- Instantiation with default parameters succeeds: `TripleScreenStrategy()`\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py::test_class_is_valid_strategy`\n\n---\n\n## AC2 — Screen 1: EMA slope correctly identifies trend direction\n\n### AC2.1 — Rising EMA slope → uptrend\n\n**Given** synthetic weekly bars whose close prices strictly increase over the last `trend_ema_period + 1` bars  \n**When** `_screen1_trend()` is called with those bars  \n**Then** the return value is `\"UP\"`\n\n### AC2.2 — Falling EMA slope → downtrend\n\n**Given** synthetic weekly bars whose close prices strictly decrease  \n**When** `_screen1_trend()` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `\"DOWN\"`\n\n### AC2.3 — Insufficient weekly bars → None\n\n**Given** fewer than `trend_ema_period + 1` synthetic weekly bars  \n**When** `_screen1_trend()` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `None`\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py -k \"screen1\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC3 — Screen 2: Stochastic oscillator activates correctly\n\n### AC3.1 — Uptrend + oversold %K → screen activated\n\n**Given** a candle series where the last few closes are near the period low (deep pullback)  \n  and trend is `\"UP\"`  \n**When** `_screen2_oscillator()` is called  \n**Then** the screen returns `True` (buy setup confirmed)\n\n### AC3.2 — Uptrend + %K above oversold threshold → screen not activated\n\n**Given** a candle series where %K is above `stoch_oversold`  \n  and trend is `\"UP\"`  \n**When** `_screen2_oscillator()` is called  \n**Then** the screen returns `False`\n\n### AC3.3 — Downtrend + overbought %K → screen activated\n\n**Given** a candle series where the last few closes are near the period high (rally in downtrend)  \n  and trend is `\"DOWN\"`  \n**When** `_screen2_oscillator()` is called  \n**Then** the screen returns `True` (short setup confirmed)\n\n### AC3.4 — Downtrend + %K below overbought threshold → screen not activated\n\n**Given** a candle series where %K is below `stoch_overbought`  \n  and trend is `\"DOWN\"`  \n**When** `_screen2_oscillator()` is called  \n**Then** the screen returns `False`\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py -k \"screen2\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC4 — Screen 3: Breakout trigger fires correctly\n\n### AC4.1 — Uptrend + breakout above prior high → LONG trigger\n\n**Given** trend is `\"UP\"`, Screen 2 activated, and `current_price > kline_data[-2][\"high\"]`  \n**When** `_screen3_trigger()` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `True`\n\n### AC4.2 — Uptrend + no breakout → no trigger\n\n**Given** trend is `\"UP\"`, Screen 2 activated, but `current_price <= kline_data[-2][\"high\"]`  \n**When** `_screen3_trigger()` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `False`\n\n### AC4.3 — Downtrend + breakout below prior low → SHORT trigger\n\n**Given** trend is `\"DOWN\"`, Screen 2 activated, and `current_price < kline_data[-2][\"low\"]`  \n**When** `_screen3_trigger()` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `True`\n\n### AC4.4 — Downtrend + no breakout → no trigger\n\n**Given** trend is `\"DOWN\"`, Screen 2 activated, but `current_price >= kline_data[-2][\"low\"]`  \n**When** `_screen3_trigger()` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `False`\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py -k \"screen3\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC5 — Combined: `generate_signal` produces correct decisions\n\n### AC5.1 — All three screens pass (uptrend) → LONG signal\n\n**Given** deterministic kline_data where:\n- EMA slope is rising (Screen 1 = UP)\n- Stochastic %K < `stoch_oversold` (Screen 2 activated)\n- `current_price > kline_data[-2][\"high\"]` (Screen 3 triggered)\n\n**When** `strategy.generate_signal(kline_data, \"BTC-USD\", \"4h\", current_price)` is called  \n**Then**:\n- Return value is a `TradingSignal` (not None)\n- `signal.decision == \"LONG\"`\n- `signal.confidence` is in `[0.1, 1.0]`\n- `signal.entry_price == current_price`\n- `signal.stop_loss == current_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct)` (within float tolerance)\n- `signal.take_profit == current_price * (1 + take_profit_pct)` (within float tolerance)\n- `signal.reasoning` contains \"Screen\" (screens are named in the reasoning string)\n\n### AC5.2 — All three screens pass (downtrend) → SHORT signal\n\n**Given** deterministic kline_data where:\n- EMA slope is falling (Screen 1 = DOWN)\n- Stochastic %K > `stoch_overbought` (Screen 2 activated)\n- `current_price < kline_data[-2][\"low\"]` (Screen 3 triggered)\n\n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then**:\n- `signal.decision == \"SHORT\"`\n- `signal.stop_loss == current_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct)`\n- `signal.take_profit == current_price * (1 - take_profit_pct)`\n\n### AC5.3 — Screen 1 passes but Screen 2 does not activate → `None`\n\n**Given** EMA slope rising (UP) but stochastic %K is well above `stoch_oversold`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then** return value is `None`\n\n### AC5.4 — Screens 1 and 2 pass but Screen 3 does not fire → `None`\n\n**Given** EMA slope rising (UP), %K below `stoch_oversold`, but `current_price <= kline_data[-2][\"high\"]`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then** return value is `None`\n\n### AC5.5 — Fewer than min candles → `None` without exception\n\n**Given** `len(kline_data) < weekly_bars * (trend_ema_period + 1) + stoch_k_period + stoch_d_period`  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called  \n**Then** return value is `None` and no exception is raised\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py -k \"generate_signal\"`\n\n---\n\n## AC6 — Non-HOLD signals are generated in a realistic market scenario\n\n**Given** a synthetic 200-candle 4h dataset designed with a clear trend + pullback + breakout pattern  \n**When** `generate_signal()` is called on the last candle  \n**Then** the return value is a `TradingSignal` (not `None`), proving the strategy is not permanently stuck in HOLD\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py::test_generates_signal_in_realistic_scenario`\n\n---\n\n## AC7 — Reference backtest completes without crash and PnL is calculated\n\n**Given** a test environment with:\n- PostgreSQL or SQLite database configured\n- Market data available for BTCUSD, timeframe 4h, 2024-01-01 to 2024-03-31\n\n**When** the reference backtest from `QuantAgent-vna-IM` is run:\n```python\nstrategy = TripleScreenStrategy()\nbacktest = Backtest(\n    start_date=datetime(2024, 1, 1),\n    end_date=datetime(2024, 3, 31),\n    assets=[\"BTC-USD\"],\n    timeframe=\"4h\",\n    initial_capital=100_000.0,\n    strategy=strategy,\n)\nmetrics = backtest.run(name=\"QuantAgent-vna-reference\")\n```\n\n**Then**:\n- `backtest.run()` completes without raising any exception\n- `metrics.total_pnl` is a finite float (positive, negative, or zero)\n- `metrics.total_trades >= 0`\n- The run is logged with a name containing \"QuantAgent-vna\"\n\n**Testable:** Manual integration test or `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py::test_backtest_integration -m integration`\n\n---\n\n## AC8 — `should_reevaluate` always returns False\n\n**Given** any `ActivePosition` and `current_price`  \n**When** `strategy.should_reevaluate(position, current_price)` is called  \n**Then** the return value is `False`\n\n**Testable:** `pytest tests/test_triple_screen_strategy.py::test_should_reevaluate_false`\n\n---\n\n## Non-goals (explicitly excluded)\n\n- Performance targets (win rate, Sharpe ratio, drawdown)\n- Multi-symbol parallel backtesting validation\n- Provider-specific behaviour or LLM integration\n- Comparison against RSI or LLMAgentStrategy results\n","numLines":221,"startLine":1,"totalLines":221}}}
