{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01AbBayUrVYob5HjTdfRUdcs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the codebase and the documentation patterns. I'm ready to create the planning artifacts for QuantAgent-b8r:\n\n1. `docs/01_requirements/QuantAgent-b8r-RQ-52week-high-momentum.md` - Requirements\n2. `docs/03_design/QuantAgent-b8r-DS-52week-high-momentum.md` - Design\n3. `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-b8r-AC-52week-high-momentum.md` - Acceptance Tests\n\n\n4. I need to set up the artifacts directory, update the README files across the documentation folders, and add the final Beads comment.\n\nThe strategy centers on the 52-week high momentum concept from George & Hwang 2004, where the price-to-52-week-high ratio serves as the key signal for identifying breakout opportunities and positive momentum patterns.\n\nImplementing the strategy logic... Looking at the remaining parameters and minimum candle requirements, I need to verify the data window needed for the strategy to function properly—the rolling maximum for the 52-week high requires at least 253 candles, and combined with the trend filter, I'm ensuring we have sufficient historical data before generating signals.\n\nNow I'm laying out the entry logic: first I calculate the 52-week high from the lookback window, then apply the trend and volume moving averages to filter for uptrend conditions before checking if price is near or breaking above that resistance level.\n\nFor confidence scoring, I'm measuring how far above the 52-week high we are and normalizing that to a 0.1 to 1.0 range. Since this is a long-only momentum strategy, I'm only generating long signals without shorts, and exits will rely on trailing stops or custom exit conditions.\n\nNow I'm setting up the planning artifacts with the appropriate file naming convention and checking the imports in the strategy module.","signature":""}],"stop_r