{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01CgmHyodvztpjD2vaPZ48zc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a complete picture of the codebase. I need to look at how `Backtest` is used to understand the reference backtest profile for this strategy. But I already have enough context to write the planning docs. Let me also quickly check what tests look like for QuantAgent-vna to get the pattern.\n\nLet me now create the planning artifacts:\n\n1. Requirements doc (RQ)\n2. Design doc (DS)  \n3. Acceptance tests doc (AC)\n4. Update README files in the three docs directories\n5. Create artifacts dir files (result.json, run-report.md, quality-gates.log)\n\n\n6. Add Beads comment\n\nFor the strategy itself, I'm settling on long-only positioning since the issue specifies that constraint unless the planner justifies otherwise, which keeps scope tight and aligns with the George & Hwang (2004) research on momentum near 52-week highs. The core signal will be proximity-based — triggering when price is within a certain percentage of the 52-week high, like 5%.\n\nActually, reconsidering the George & Hwang findings: the real edge comes from stocks *approaching* their 52-week high rather than breaking through it, since traders anchor to that reference point and create buying pressure as the price nears it. So for M1, I'll use a breakout above the 52-week high as the primary entry signal for simplicity and clarity, with proximity as a secondary option. I'll add a trend filter checking that price is above the 50-day moving average to confirm momentum.\n\nFor the backtest setup, I need to pull US equities like AAPL and MSFT on daily timeframes, running from early 2022 through 2023 to ensure I have enough historical data—at least 252 days for the 52-week lookback plus additional days for the 50-day trend calculation and a proper testing window.\n\nSetting up the backtest configuration...\n\nI need to create the artifacts directory first before writing out the planning documents, so let me check if it exists and create it if necessary.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2522,"cache_read_input_tokens":53821,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2522},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e29365a-7925-40eb-8646-1f5eb6603bf2","uuid":"b131d596-af25-40ce-8eb6-d58fe7c914a3"}
